>
  <p>
    <strong>We couldn't find a public Zen Planner help page with the steps for exporting a member list</strong>, so we're not going to
    guess at them here. This is what we could confirm on November 6, 2026.
  </p>
  <h2>What Zen Planner says</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Its reporting page says reports can be exported to Excel.</li>
    <li>
      Its help center says reporting won't return more than 2,000 records, so a list longer than that has to be filtered down.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What another company's guide says</h2>
  <p>
    Gymdesk, another software company, publishes a migration guide that says to go to <strong>New Report</strong> and choose
    <strong>People</strong>. That report includes leads and contacts as well as members. This isn't Zen Planner's own documentation
    and we haven't tested it, so confirm it with Zen Planner support if your screen looks different.
  </p>
  <p>
    Once you have the file, save it as a CSV and keep only your current members. BeltManager only accepts active and trial students,
    and it needs first name, last name and date of birth.
  </p>
  <h2>Payment data</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We found no Zen Planner page that says what payment data you can export or what that costs, so we make no claim about it.</strong>
    If you want your payment history or stored card details moved, ask Zen Planner in writing what it will provide and whether there's
    a fee before you make plans around it. The import below doesn't need any payment data.
  </p>
</ExportGuideLayout>
